      "writtenOn": "2025-03-05T16:54:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e are suspecting calls into IHalAdapterVendorExtension service might be delayed?\n\nAnything can happen. It\u0027s better to limit the scope of locking to the minimum possible operations.\n\n\u003e I feel passing mutex outside the class, breaks simplicity.\n\u003e\n\u003e I could break functions ParseAnd... so that only calls into IModule and IStream* are serialized.\n\nThe common pattern in STL is to pass a mutex wrapped into `unique_lock` (`std::unique_lock\u003cstd::mutex\u003e\u0026`) so that both the caller and callee can see what is the state of the mutex (locked or not). I think that\u0027s totally fine.\n\nYou can try and see which approach produces simpler code.\n\n\u003e Are you also saying we should serialize all IModule calls like how we did for IStream* ones?\n\nNot all, only the part dealing with parameters (since we anyway have to change `parseAndSetVendorParameters` to operate the lock). All other calls are naturally serialized due to the fact that they are handled via `Hal2AidlMapper` access to which is serialized.",
      "parentUuid": "ec82f833_462eb837",
